    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d331">

                <pb facs="0657" n="561" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg561"/>

                <head>No. 329.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Sir Edward Thornton to Mr.
                    Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-06-19"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 19, 1874</date>.
                        (Received June 20.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In compliance with an instruction from the
                    Earl of Derby, I have the honor to inclose copy of a dispatch addressed to his
                    lordship by Her Majesty’s consul-general at Tripoli, in which he expresses his
                    opinion that the slave traffic from Tripoli to Constantinople via Malta is on
                    the decrease, and that there is no reason whatever for supposing that the Malta
                    police authorities in any way connive at its existence.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>EDW’D THORNTON.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d331-a1.xml" xpointer="d331-a1"/>
            </div>
